// The wire models, generated by openapi-generator from spec/openapi.yaml. Only
// this file is hand-written; scripts/generate.sh replaces models/ wholesale.
//
// They carry the spec's optionality and NULLABILITY exactly - `update_freq:
// Option<String>` for a field that may be missing, `expires: Option<..>` behind
// `Option::deserialize` for one that is always present and may be null - which
// no hand-written struct would stay honest about across a spec change. The
// idiomatic layer re-exports them rather than mapping into parallel structs, so
// a spec change reaches a consumer without a hand-edited mapper.
//
// The generator's REQUEST functions are deliberately not taken; scripts/
// generate.sh says why, and transport.rs is what replaces them.
//
// The spec still carries the legacy v1 endpoints, so their schemas are here too
// and are dead code: this crate targets v2 alone. Stripping them would mean
// editing the pinned spec, which is the one file that must stay byte-identical
// to what was published.
//
// Generated code is held to the generator's standards, not ours.
#![allow(clippy::all, dead_code, unused_imports)]

pub mod models;
